# 1. Mission and scope

This document defines the complete backend target for HOMIO / REOS.

The objective is to make the backend a secure, scalable, AI-enabled and automation-first real-estate operating platform—not simply a collection of APIs or Python modules.

The backend must support the complete business lifecycle:

**Identity → Tenant → Builder/Inventory Acquisition → Property Verification → Search → Enquiry → Lead Qualification → Ownership Attribution → Communication → Site Visit → Deal → Trust/Fraud Governance → Commission → Settlement → Reconciliation → Reporting.**

It must also support broker SaaS, builder SaaS, enterprise/white-label, platform/API partners, AI-driven customer assistance, analytics, international expansion, operational automation and recoverable workflows.

## 1.1 Scope exclusion

Only frontend visual UI/UX delivery is excluded from this backend scope:

- Page layouts and visual components.
- CSS and design tokens.
- Animations and visual effects.
- Responsive styling and presentation.
- Frontend visual refinements.

The following are **not excluded**:

- Backend API architecture and implementation.
- API request/response schemas.
- Authentication, session, authorization and tenant boundaries.
- Database and persistence.
- Search and AI integration.
- Backend business workflows.
- Security and privacy.
- Frontend-to-backend API contracts.
- Backend integration and end-to-end tests.
- Deployment, monitoring, recovery and production readiness.

The separate frontend owner may build the UI. Backend APIs and integration contracts must still be complete and production-safe.

